title: Using plugins
order: 0
---
# Plugins

The first-party plugins are packages of their own, named `@mdsvex/plugin-*`. Each exports a function, and what it returns goes in the [`plugins`](/docs/plugins/writing/bundles) option:

```js
import { mdsvex } from 'mdsvex';
import { anchors } from '@mdsvex/plugin-anchors';
import { citations } from '@mdsvex/plugin-citations';
import { code_blocks } from '@mdsvex/plugin-code-blocks';
import { diagram } from '@mdsvex/plugin-diagram';
import { emoji } from '@mdsvex/plugin-emoji';
import { external_links } from '@mdsvex/plugin-external-links';
import { elements } from '@mdsvex/plugin-elements';
import { embeds } from '@mdsvex/plugin-embeds';
import { figures } from '@mdsvex/plugin-figures';
import { link_check } from '@mdsvex/plugin-link-check';
import { numbering } from '@mdsvex/plugin-numbering';
import { page_data } from '@mdsvex/plugin-page-data';
import { references } from '@mdsvex/plugin-references';
import { steps } from '@mdsvex/plugin-steps';
import { tabs } from '@mdsvex/plugin-tabs';
import { toc } from '@mdsvex/plugin-toc';

mdsvex({
	heading_ids: true,
	plugins: [
		steps(),
		tabs(),
		elements(),
		embeds(),
		figures(),
		code_blocks(),
		diagram(),
		anchors(),
		external_links(),
		toc(),
		page_data(),
		references({ repo: 'you/site' }),
		emoji(),
		citations(),
		numbering(),
		link_check({ routes: 'src/routes' })
	]
});
```

| package | what it adds |
| --- | --- |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-steps`](/docs/plugins/steps) | numbered steps, one for each heading inside `:::steps` |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-tabs`](/docs/plugins/tabs) | tabs and code groups, one tab for each heading or code fence inside `:::tabs` |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-elements`](/docs/plugins/elements) | details, accordions, keys, ruby, badges, marks, insertions and abbreviations, each a directive over an HTML element |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-embeds`](/docs/plugins/embeds) | YouTube and Vimeo players named by their title |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-code-blocks`](/docs/plugins/code-blocks) | a `pre` with a copy button, the title and the caption of the fence |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-diagram`](/docs/plugins/diagrams) | `mermaid` fences drawn by pele at build time or by mermaid in the browser |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-figures`](/docs/plugins/figures) | `:::figure[Caption]` around an image or anything else, numbered when a numbering plugin asks |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-anchors`](/docs/plugins/anchors) | a link to itself on every heading that has an id |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-external-links`](/docs/plugins/external-links) | `rel` and `target` on every link that leaves the site |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-toc`](/docs/plugins/toc) | the headings of a document as data, and a `::toc` directive that lists them |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-page-data`](/docs/plugins/page-data) | a reading time, an excerpt, an inferred title, an edit url and a last modified date for each document |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-emoji`](/docs/plugins/emoji) | emoji shortcodes, `:tada:` becomes the emoji, with an optional label for screen readers |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-references`](/docs/plugins/references) | links for `@user`, `#123`, `owner/repo#123` and commits, and for bare urls when asked |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-citations`](/docs/plugins/citations) | `:cite[key]` from a CSL JSON bibliography, and a `::bibliography` that lists what a document cites |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-link-check`](/docs/plugins/link-check) | a warning at every link to an id or a document that is not there |
| [`@mdsvex/plugin-numbering`](/docs/plugins/numbering) | numbered figures, tables, equations and sections, and `:ref[fig:x]` references that read as the number |
